Thanks @chalasr, this round found real defects. Every one was reproduced on 8.2 and on the PR head before anything changed; head is now 099fa37194b.

Fixed, each with its test:

- `ArrayInput` named keys became segments: `['command' => 'deploy', 'target' => 'rollback']` ran `deploy:rollback` with `target` unset. `getUnparsedTokens()` now puts a `--` in front of the first string-keyed parameter, so a named argument can never name a sub-command, and option parameters keep their place before it.
- `false` option values: re-emitting now follows the convention of `Input::unparse()`, so `--ansi => false` becomes `--no-ansi`, a value-less option set to false is not re-emitted at all, and a value option keeps its `=value` form.
- `help` resolved every lazy command: both `getNamespaces()` calls are gone, replaced by `all($path)` which resolves the sub-tree only. In my probe with six lazy commands, `help app:one nope` went from 6 to 1 and `help other` from 6 to 1.
- A command re-running itself received the outer chain: the chain is reused only when its last level holds the very input being run.
- The chain survived a throwing command: `try`/`finally` now. `$runningCommand` stays out of it on purpose, since `renderThrowable()` prints the synopsis of the command that failed.
- The bare namespace holding only hidden commands rendered the application header before throwing: the listing is built in a buffer and written only once it succeeded.
- An alias resolving outside its own namespace orphaned the sub-commands registered under it: the alias is canonicalized unless that would orphan them, so `docker compose up` reaches `docker:compose:up` while `docker compose` still runs the aliased command.
- The application options replayed on the leaf keep the token as it was given, so `docker -vv compose up` reaches the leaf as `-vv`, `hasParameterOption('-vv')` included.

Documentation: `UPGRADE-8.2.md` gained the Console section it was missing, covering the sub-command-first rule in both forms, the positional `ArrayInput` binding, the bare-namespace `ConsoleEvents::ERROR` removal and the collapsed listing. The description now names the colon form in the behavior-change list, says that `--format=json` and `--format=md` keep listing every command, and states what the option replay really promises.

The level-arguments point is the one I did not apply; the reasoning is in that thread, and I am happy to go the other way if you prefer the narrower chain API.

